From c5f152ba02967f5958eee29841eb51b04b9682ac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 02:11:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] AudioEngine/VideoPlayer: audio settings changed during
 playback apply at once

Kodi chooses when a stream opens whether it passes through and which
decoder decodes it. A change of those settings while it played reached the
audio engine but not the stream: it kept passing through after passthrough
was turned off for its format, and stayed decoded after it was turned on,
until the next video.

- CVideoPlayerAudio registers for the settings of passthrough (on/off, the
  output configuration, each format, the DTS-HD core) and for the dynamic
  range compression of Dolby Digital, and at the next frame looks at the
  codec again, as it does when the display is reset. A setting of
  passthrough also changes which passthrough (all of DTS-HD, or its core); the
  compression opens a decoder of AC-3/E-AC-3 again (one frame of sound is
  lost: FFmpeg has no way to change it while it decodes). kodi.log says what
  changed.
- CActiveAE::SupportsRaw() and UsesDtsCoreFallback() read the settings as
  they are, not the engine's copy, which its own thread reloads later: the
  player that asks right after a change gets the new answer.
- The engine's resampler is made again when the upmix of stereo or the LFE
  in a downmix changes, as it was for the quality and the normalisation:
  ConfigureResampler() was given both and kept neither.

The decisions are in AudioSettingsLive.h, tested on the host. Not at once,
on purpose: the passthrough device (the engine moves the sound to it at once;
which formats it takes is known only once it is open) and passthrough of live
streams (it decides how the player follows the source's clock).

Idea: the live audio settings of pannal's CoreELEC builds (p3i T4c); written
anew.
